gg Video","original":"pedestrian_crossing_TNA_56K.wmv","md5":"e56bffed816662a46fecf0f00cb14455","mtime":"1227854613","size":"7220501","crc32":"eeecdd1e","sha1":"5e8056899fae03ca48c672c5a102b19f388023c3","length":"123.13","height":"304","width":"400"},{"name":"pedestrian_crossing_TNA_56K.wmv","source":"original","format":"Windows Media","md5":"12c1ed8bb939809ec1a74221bc16caf5","mtime":"1129584295","size":"776597","crc32":"ec6fb7d0","sha1":"87af910a7c560e1ec0403d5256769176c07cc34f","length":"124.47","height":"288","width":"352"},{"name":"pedestrian_crossing_TNA_56K_512kb.mp4","source":"derivative","format":"512Kb MPEG4","original":"pedestrian_crossing_TNA_56K.wmv","md5":"b453fc65d3c8a13c9e6837e56f66fca3","mtime":"1227854765","size":"8541425","crc32":"95f4d8c6","sha1":"04cae3451369312eb72a29f77a945540fc21da11","length":"124.04","height":"240","width":"320"},{"name":"pedestrian_crossing_TNA_archive.torrent","source":"metadata","btih":"bc0b13f15bb75314cf1a141f08a72093b146efbd","mtime":"1547530036","size":"11434","md5":"8714406b2355450a5201ff21459af434","crc32":"fdbe7f2d","sha1":"1d421cff6271d6fef53d22c3a7d1abe5e04ebaaa","format":"Archive BitTorrent"},{"name":"pedestrian_crossing_TNA_files.xml","source":"metadata","format":"Metadata","md5":"fbcda8cdd469c0fdfe17b582a3ef8947","summation":"md5"},{"name":"pedestrian_crossing_TNA_meta.xml","source":"metadata","format":"Metadata","mtime":"1547530034","size":"1169","md5":"c7afe335c1009a67065ca9db0b4b0238","crc32":"9ae3835b","sha1":"4b882a9c62631cad9c5c1fdaf6bab1a42e5f6b36"},{"name":"pedestrian_crossing_TNA_reviews.xml","source":"metadata","format":"Metadata","mtime":"1351488933","size":"3441","md5":"034c6bacddb0375aa9609585816ae061","crc32":"fccbe46e","sha1":"4f4a45bc7135555b5b543dc2a73df3057fa96dfe"}],"files_count":32,"item_last_updated":1710063331,"item_size":200979797,"metadata":{"identifier":"pedestrian_crossing_TNA","title":"Pedestrian Crossing","mediatype":"movies","collection":["british_gov_public_films","ephemera"],"subject":"road safety","description":"Humorous road safety trailer on the correct use of pedestrian crossings. Belisha beacons","date":"1948","hidden":"true","publicdate":"2005-10-10 00:19:59","addeddate":"2005-10-10 07:19:57","uploader":"florian@archive.org","sponsor":"Central Office of Information for Ministry of Transport","director":"Michael Law","publisher":"Public Relationship Films","sound":"sound","color":"color","runtime":"8:15","credits":"Public Information Films","rights":"UK Crown Copyright","language":"english","coverage":"Great Britain","updatedate":"2005-10-10 00:21:44","updater":"nVIR","backup_location":"ia903600_10","ia_orig__runtime":"8 Minutes 15 Seconds"},"reviews":[{"reviewbody":"Some amusing facial expressions at the beginning as the man thinks about thing he likes and dislikes. Then surreal scenes as he sits at a table and then lies in a bed on the crossing. It's slightly alarming that a vehicle knocks him down even when he seems to be crossing correctly.","reviewtitle":"Python-esque","stars":"4","reviewer":"rgs_uk","createdate":"2005-10-12 10:57:48","reviewdate":"2005-10-12 10:57:48"},{"reviewbody":"I find it amusing that you even have to have a film on how to cross the street, but I found it really humorous. Well written with great acting.","reviewtitle":"Who says instructional films have to be boring?","reviewer":"elocina","reviewdate":"2007-03-23 18:22:36","createdate":"2007-03-23 18:22:36","stars":"5"},{"reviewbody":"I don't know who this guy was, but he was in a LOT of these films, looks like he did a lot of his own stunt work too.. Anyways, in this, he learns to cross the street... That's about it really.","reviewtitle":"Watch out!","reviewer":"Spuzz","reviewdate":"2008-03-17 21:26:06","createdate":"2008-03-17 21:26:06","stars":"3"},{"reviewbody":"This is a good example of a PSA that can be enjoyable and funny without being corny or akward. It wasn't a masterpiece of comedy, but there were some very humorous bits (taking a nap and eating breakfast in the middle of the street, among others)it was short and to the point, and the educational message came across without seeming forced.","reviewtitle":"Very good.","reviewer":"WiglafThePirate","reviewdate":"2011-01-29 21:54:50","createdate":"2011-01-29 21:54:50","stars":"4"},{"reviewbody":"Well, this was before we had the so called \"zebra crossings\" that we have today - the black and white painted stripes on the road signifying a pedestrian crossing.  The can't have been much later than this film in coming as everything else is there that we have today - notably the Belisha beacons - the flashing globes, introduced in 1934 and named after the then Minister of Transport Hore-Belisha. You can still find Belisha beacons in other parts of the world where Brits crossed the road and ran things generally - parts of India, Singapore and Hong Kong for example.","reviewtitle":"Zebra","reviewer":"Rooftopjump","reviewdate":"2012-03-29 09:27:21","createdate":"2012-03-29 09:27:21","stars":"3"},{"reviewbody":"...all those vehicles driving on the wrong side of the street.  At least as far as I'm concerned.\n \nWhile over there you have to look to the RIGHT before you step off the curb. How strange.","reviewtitle":"Not A Peep About...","reviewer":"JayKay49","reviewdate":"2012-10-29 05:35:31","createdate":"2012-10-29 05:35:31","stars":"3"}],"server":"dn600208.us.archive.org","simplelists":{"solo_manifest":{"solo_manifest_dn600208":{"sys_changed_by":{"source":"task","task_id":"5421459051"},"sys_last_changed":"2026-06-06 15:23:25.821101"}}},"solo":true,"uniq":1627424568,"workable_servers":["dn600208.us.archive.org"]}